  "id": "paced-auditory-serial-addition-test",
  "term": "Paced Auditory Serial Addition Test",
  "definition": "The Paced Auditory Serial Addition Test (PASAT) is a cognitive test used to evaluate cognitive functioning in research, including studies of people with multiple sclerosis. In this context, it is one of several measures used to assess cognitive outcomes alongside other memory and processing tests.",
